-- title:
--   Twisting the Tate slot parameter by ζ modulo ζ-1
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a commutative ring, let $p$ and $j$ be natural numbers with $0 < j$ and $j < p$, let $c$ and $\zeta$ be units of $K$, and let $n$ be a natural number. Here [`ModularCurve.tateUnivX`](def/ModularCurve_TateSlots.html#L10) is the two-variable power series over $\mathbb Z$ whose coefficient at an exponent $e = (e_0,e_1)$ is $-2\sum_{d \mid e_1} d$ when $e_0 = e_1$, and otherwise is $|e_0 - e_1|$ if $|e_0-e_1|$ divides $e_1$ and $0$ if it does not; and for a unit $b$ of $K$, [`ModularCurve.slotSubst K p b j`](def/ModularCurve_TateSlots.html#L31) is the one-variable power series over $K$ obtained by substituting the family $\bigl(\mathrm C(b)\,X^{j},\ \mathrm C(b^{-1})\,X^{\,p-j}\bigr)$ for the two variables. The assertion is that for every $n$ the difference of the $n$-th coefficients
--   $$\operatorname{coeff}_n\bigl(\mathrm{slotSubst}\,K\,p\,(\zeta c)\,j\ \mathrm{tateUnivX}\bigr) - \operatorname{coeff}_n\bigl(\mathrm{slotSubst}\,K\,p\,c\,j\ \mathrm{tateUnivX}\bigr)$$
--   lies in the ideal of $K$ generated by $(\zeta : K) - 1$.
--
--   The series $\mathrm{slotSubst}\,K\,p\,c\,j\ \mathrm{tateUnivX}$ is the $X$-coordinate, as a power series in the Tate parameter, of the point with parameter $u = c\,q^{j}$ on the Tate curve with parameter $q^{p}$; the statement says that replacing $c$ by $\zeta c$ perturbs every coefficient by a multiple of $\zeta - 1$, with no primality or root-of-unity hypothesis on $\zeta$. It is used in the construction of level automorphisms with prescribed valuation behaviour at auxiliary level, in [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_isLevelAutAt_mem_chartAlgFin_mem_nonunits_gaussValuationSubring_and_apply_not_mem`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_isLevelAutAt_mem_chartAlgFin_mem_nonunits_gaussValuationSubring_and_apply_not_mem).
-- source:
